@verbs consent consentir
@tier player
@title deciding what others may do to you

There are things another player cannot do to you unless you allow
them. Each of those is a consent, set to yes or no, and every one
of them starts at no. The verb is not translated yet:

  consentir                       lists how you have them now.
  consentir <name> sí             allows it.
  consentir <name> no             stops allowing it.

The consents, by the names you type, are:

  dar             somebody giving you an object.
  proteger        somebody protecting you in a fight.
  grupos          being taken into an adventuring party.
  invitaciones    being bought a drink.
  autoequiparse   equipping yourself on entering the game.
  seguir          somebody following you.
  resucitar       somebody bringing you back to life.

Anybody trying something you do not consent to is refused. With
'dar', on top of that, you are told they tried.
